util/rust: resolve the bindgen wrapper's include from the build root

bindgen writes the wrapper for static inline functions (util_bindings.c)
with an #include of its input header spelled relative to the directory it
ran in, which is the build root:

    #include "../mesa-<sha>/src/util/rust/util_bindgen.h"

The static_library() compiling that wrapper only passes inc_util, so the
path resolves only by accident: with a build directory inside the source
tree it is "../src/util/rust/util_bindgen.h", and "<src>/include/.." happens
to be the source root.  With the build directory beside the source tree, as
Portage lays it out, nothing on the include path has the build root's
parent as its own parent and the compile dies with "No such file or
directory".

Every other output_inline_wrapper user in the tree (compiler/rust, nvk,
rusticl, kraid) already adds the build root to the wrapper's include
directories.  Do the same here.

Introduced by 9fc5a89863 ("util/rust: Add bindgen for
pipe_format/util_format_*."), 2026-11-11.  Not upstream as of cca2fd7f.

--- a/src/util/rust/meson.build
+++ b/src/util/rust/meson.build
@@ -54,7 +54,10 @@
 libutil_rust_bindgen_c = static_library(
   'util_rust_bindgen_c',
   _util_rust_bindgen[1],
-  include_directories : inc_util,
+  include_directories : [
+    fs.relative_to(meson.project_build_root(), meson.current_source_dir()),
+    inc_util,
+  ],
   dependencies : [
     idep_mesautil.partial_dependency(compile_args : true, includes : true,
                                      sources : true),
